Let $x$ be an integer such that $50 < x < 100$ and $x \equiv 3 \pmod{7}$.
Since $x \equiv 3 \pmod{7}$, $x$ can be written as $x = 7k + 3$ for some integer $k$.
Substituting $50 < x < 100$, we have $50 < 7k + 3 < 100$.
Subtracting 3, we get $47 < 7k < 97$.
Dividing by 7, we get $\frac{47}{7} < k < \frac{97}{7}$, which means $6.71 < k < 13.86$.
Since $k$ must be an integer, $7 \le k \le 13$.

Therefore, $x = 7k + 3$ can be:
$k=7: x = 7(7) + 3 = 49 + 3 = 52$
$k=8: x = 7(8) + 3 = 56 + 3 = 59$
$k=9: x = 7(9) + 3 = 63 + 3 = 66$
$k=10: x = 7(10) + 3 = 70 + 3 = 73$
$k=11: x = 7(11) + 3 = 77 + 3 = 80$
$k=12: x = 7(12) + 3 = 84 + 3 = 87$
$k=13: x = 7(13) + 3 = 91 + 3 = 94$
